  "coverage": {
    "closed_over": "the audit tree as it stands when this ledger was generated",
    "why_not_a_closure_assertion_over_the_live_tree": "The audit job appends one genuine independent audit to the audit tree after every successful producer dispatch (frontier-team.yml: audit job runs `if: needs.team.result == 'success'`, and its output is merged into the accepted base). The producer therefore NEVER sees its own run's audit and the tree it sees grows by one file per dispatch. Schema v1 asserted that this committed ledger equalled a fresh build over the live tree; that assertion was unsatisfiable by construction and made the suite red on every dispatch. The ledger is now an append-only RECORD: every file it names must still exist with the recorded sha256 (nothing edited, nothing deleted), and files it does not name yet are reported as UNDISCLOSED rather than treated as corruption. See results/frontier/<team>/AUDIT_TREE_PROVENANCE.schema.md."
  },
