      "why": "This file carries the COMPLETE independent-audit signature (required_fixes + safe_to_integrate + team) and no artifact_provenance_warning, so the contract's signature-based routing classifies it as an audit of record. It was in fact written by this team. No test reading the file can tell the difference -- that is the residual weakness declared in run 38848314260, now realised in the live tree. The file is left byte-for-byte untouched (rule 6: never overwrite or delete a claim-bearing historical artifact) and is NOT to be read as an independent gate. It is also, as of the run 38852056955 repair, barred from satisfying the anti-vacuity invariant that requires a genuine audit of record to exist."
    }
